CONCLUSIONS (source analysis, not phone/electrical results)

The selected vendor DTS describes OTG ID on TLMM110, SMB1360 at QUP4 I2C0x14,
and that charger as the VBUS regulator. Its OTG regulator changes CMD_CHG_REG
0x42 bit0, preserving charging-enable bit1. Its input-presence path is inverse
USBIN undervoltage status at0x54 bit0. These are precise missing mainline device
operations, not evidence that the controller lacks dual-role capability.

A new SMB1360-specific driver/binding must own the device coherently: required
initialization and shared-register synchronization, regulator state/control,
input presence if independent PM8916 sensing is not proved, and fault handling.
No invented PMIC VBUS rail or optional FET route is justified. Do not port the
whole charger/fuel-gauge policy merely to get boost, or depend silently on
bootloader configuration. First determine the documented minimum safe setup.

Source proves neither measured5V at the connector nor safe charging/boost
arbitration. The selected1500mA threshold is BATTERY current, not USB output
current. The code does not interpret UVLO encoding2 in millivolts. OTG startup
advances after a timer, not proved voltage measurement. These remain test and
hardware-documentation requirements before enabling output.

