UVLO: OTG_UVLO_REG0x12, bits4:2 mask0x1c, code2 shifted2 => value0x08
(C:116-119,3812-3819). Source gives no mV mapping.
D:53 float-voltage-mv4400 is BATTERY CHARGING voltage via0x15 (C:770-787), not VBUS.
No output voltage operation/readback exists in this regulator.
U:731-739: A_WAIT_VRISE timer says "TODO: use vbus_vld interrupt", then sets
A_VBUS_VLD. Source host progression therefore is not measured5V proof.

STATUS / FAULTS / INTERRUPTS

IRQ_F_REG0x55 (C:195,2227-2243,2298-2356): two-bit-per-event layout:
  power_ok: RTbit0/latchbit1
  otg_fail: RTbit4/latchbit5
  otg_oc:   RTbit6/latchbit7
C:2094-2115 handles fail/OC by unconditionally clearing OTG0x42 bit0, even on
falling status transitions. No retry, regulator fault notification, or direct
USB FSM notification; IRQ handling later notifies battery power_supply_changed.
USB vbus_is_on cache/regulator use count can thus diverge from hardware after
fault shutdown. Autonomous cutoff timing and exact OTG fault IRQ enables are
not established by this source. A port must address fault-state reconciliation,
not silently preserve the vendor's cached-success behavior.

D:51 selects stat-pulsed-irq. C:3822-3838 programs STAT0x09 mask0x1b value0x08.
C:4395-4421 requests IRQF_TRIGGER_RISING|IRQF_ONESHOT in BOTH hardware-major
branches, despite DT interrupts<62 8> (level-low). Resolve actual waveform and
intended interrupt mode, rather than blindly transplanting inconsistent flags.
Normal IRQ masks C:95-114,3840-3875:0x0f=0xc5,0x10=0xd7,0x11=0x1f. No named
OTG fault-enable bits in these masks establish further semantics. Suspend masks
are0xc4,0x07,0x0b (input UV retained); resume restores saved masks and services
deferred IRQs (C:4573-4653). Shutdown disables OTG (C:4657-4670).

INPUT PRESENCE / CHARGER INTERACTION

IRQ_E_REG0x54 bit0=USBIN_UV; bit1=latched UV event.
C:3143-3149 sets initial usb_present=!(status & BIT(0)) and calls
power_supply_set_present(usb). C:1776-1794 updates on UV interrupts.
U:4183-4187,3741-3791 maps POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_PRESENT to B_SESS_VLD. It suppresses
subsequent state-machine work with ID grounded (U:3756-3764), and clears B-session
validity on entering host (U:3336-3338). This is input-presence logic, not output
voltage measurement. A new provider must cover initial state, changes, self-VBUS
and discharge behavior, not substitute charging activity for input presence.

U:1947-1968 says notify host mode before enabling regulator; disable regulator
before notifying device mode. Comment claims charger should stop drawing input,
but the nonlegacy notifier only sets motg->host_mode and power_supply_changed
(U:1649-1675). SMB1360 callback reads CURRENT_MAX+ONLINE, not SCOPE
(C:1461-1504). Charging0x42 bit1 is independent (C:809-855), and OTG preserves it.
For requested input current<=2mA, C:1174-1186 explicitly says USB suspend is not
supported and selects minimum USB current instead. This DT omits min-icl-100ma,
so fallback is USB500,0x41 bits1:0=0 (C:1108-1134).
Inference, NOT proof: chip hardware likely supplies mode arbitration. Source
alone does not establish reverse isolation/charging interlock guarantees. Do not
assume a notification comment is an electrical safety mechanism, and do not
invent an unvalidated charging-disable sequence to fill that gap.

PM8916 CANDIDATES / NON-EVIDENCE

L:603-618 can sample USB RT status0x1310 bit1; msm-pm8916.dtsi:250-257 defines
its USBIN IRQ<0 0x13 1>. But selected D:74-77 sets use-external-charger;
L:2608-2636,2696-2699 disables LBC and returns-ENODEV before USB initialization,
initial status or IRQ registration. The disabling helper L:2293-2308 writes:
  charger0x1049 mask0x81 value1
  BATIF0x1249 mask0xf0 value0
  BPD0x1248 value0x09
It does not touch USB peripheral0x1300. This proves neither unavailable PMIC
sensing nor connected/working sensing. Mainline has a separate PM8916 USBIN
extcon driver: see baseline companion note. Do not enable its LBC charger.

msm8939-common.dtsi:1693-1703 declares VADC channel0 usb_in, but USB voltage
getter U:4117-4134 asks for "usbin" VADC. drivers/hwmon/qpnp-adc-voltage.c:
1430-1445 requires qcom,usbin-vadc and returns-ENODEV if absent. No8939 DT has
that phandle; it appears only on other8226/8974 variants. Thus this selected
release DT does not provide that getter a VADC handle. SMB1360's own VADC phandle
is used for BATTERY ID (C:3930-3938,3974-3979), not VBUS. Neither declaration nor
getter proves actual connector-VBUS measurement or wiring.

